    portfast can only be enabled on access ports which allows it to immediately transition to a forwarding state
    ports with both BPDUguard and portfast will shutdown if they receive a BPDU
    RootGuard enforces root placement and prevents hijackings like this from happening        

Lab 1.4 (DHCP starvation & DNS spoofing)
Lab Setup:
SW1
R1:
    ip dhcp exclude-address 192.168.1.1
    ip dhcp pool IP_POOL
    network 192.168.1.0 255.255.255.128
    lease 2
    default-router 192.168.1.1

    interface g0/0/1
    ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
    no shutdown

Attack:
Attacker/Kali:
    exhaust the IP pool with dhcpig 
    run msfconsole dhcp server right after
    once the target has been intercepted, attacks like DNSspoofing are possible using DNSchef

Defense:
    to prevent the actual exhasution of IP addresses:
        use port security on switches to prevent exhaustion through MAC flooding
        enable ip dhcp snooping on switches to allow the switch to inspect DHCP packets and enable mac verification to check if the L2 source MAC matches the DHCP client MAC field
    DHCP snooping
        ip dhcp snooping
        ip dhcp snooping <vlan-id>
    MAC address verification (matches the L2 source MAC to the DHCP Client MAC)
        ip dhcp snooping verify mac-address
    interface specific ratelimiting
        (config-if)# ip dhcp snooping limit rate <rate>
  
    untrusted ports in dhcp snooping means that the switch will stop/drop DHCP response messages(Offer,Ack,Nck) coming from those ports 
    trust interface
        (config-if)# ip dhcp snooping trust
    
    switches with DHCP snooping enabled will automatically insert an option-82 (VLAN,Port number and MAC address of client) into the DHCP packets and leave teh relay agent IP blank
    DHCP packets without relay agent IPs and have option-82 will be discarded by receiving relay agents or routers, to solve, useL
    ip dhcp relay information trust-all
    or
    (config-if)# ip dhcp relay information trusted
    to allow the packet through on the agents/routers or disable option-82 on the snooping switch
    no ip dhcp snooping information option
    
snooping switchs maintain a binding table of assigned dhcp address on untrusted ports with ACK messages adding to the table and NACK/Release/Decline removing entries

