defence:
    to prevent the attacker from simiply changing their IP,use IP source guard with:
    (config-if)# ip verify source
    
    to protect against both IP and MAC spoofing attacks use,
    (config-if)# ip verify source mac-check
    
    commands (part 1):
    DSW1:
    ip dhcp snooping
    interface g1/0/23
    ip verify source mac-check
    
     ip source binding 74D4.DD81.5CF5 vlan 30 172.16.3.10 interface g1/0/24

    explaination:
    IP source guard requires both DHCP snooping and Port Security for IP and MAC protections. with both foundational security function enabled, IP source guard uses a Source IP-MAC-Port binding to filter traffic.
    this source IP is learnt by DHCP snooping or by manual configuration thus if only DHCP snooping is configured, only DHCP packets and assigned addresses will be allowed through, all else being filtered.
    IPSG is only supported on L2 ports (access and trunk) and can be configured with source IP filtering or both IP and MAC

    note: for some reason, port security sees the client as a port violation even if there is an ip binding, i think its because the client is connected to SW3 which is conncected the the port with port security enabled.


